{"kind":"koios.duty","id":"forming-a-reported-manuscript","office":"reporter","precondition":"A durable assignment names one supported demand lens, one event spine, a genre contract, and a bounded packet of admitted source evidence.","move":"Route prose work to the cheapest faithful provider, form one event-centered manuscript, and preserve exact source links, attribution, modality, scope, production provenance, and refusal evidence.","postcondition":"A draft linked to the assignment exists for independent editorial judgment, or a typed reporting/source/provider obstruction is recorded.","refusals":["unsupported assignment lens","no event spine","insufficient distinct reported detail","provider offer absent","provider output malformed","citation custody lost"]}

lib/management/duties/judging-accountable-publication.json:
{"kind":"koios.duty","id":"judging-accountable-publication","office":"editor-in-chief","precondition":"One exact manuscript, its deterministic standards reading, source and claim records, production provenance, and any prior failure evidence are available.","move":"Procure independent judgment from an accepted provider under a provider-validated bounded tool schema, preserve its prose report, and let deterministic Koios code invoke exactly one selected editorial tool. Free-form prose labels never create publication authority.","postcondition":"The exact manuscript has an append-only accepted, revise, or refuse judgment carrying the validated tool-selection digest; publication is possible only when submit_editorial_acceptance was selected for deterministically clear bytes.","refusals":["missing source custody","missing provider offer","provider result not accepted","manuscript digest changed","standards gate failed"]}

lib/management/contracts/liss-routed-writer-inference.json:
{"kind":"koios.bilateral-contract-interface","id":"koios-hires-liss-for-routed-writer-inference","customer":"urn:ame:koios-news","provider":"urn:ame:logical-inference-service-section","providerContract":"liss-inference-service","service":"cheapest-sufficient-reported-prose","admission":"Koios solicits the strict forward subset of free-groq, free-nim, and leader-claude for which an invocation-scoped account grant is actually injected; LISS authors the exact effects and route offer; Koios accepts only that offer with an attenuated capability.","packet":["assignment","reported-analysis genre law","bounded admitted research packet","prose output shape","replayable minimum sufficiency predicates"],"result":"Provider-authored routed completion or typed refusal, with selected tier and each provider attempt retained in provider and Koios ledgers.","authority":"Provider credentials are not Koios property. The Leader Movement Team must expressly seat account custody and grant one invocation; environment presence alone is neither custody nor authorization.","editorialSeparation":"A writer-tier completion creates only a draft. Exact-manuscript publication still requires the separately contracted leader-Claude editorial judgment.","status":"leader-claude-executing; free-groq-interface-ready-awaiting-leader-custody-and-grant; free-nim-interface-ready-awaiting-invocation-grant"}

lib/law/accountable-attention-and-publication.json:
{"kind":"koios.publication-law","id":"accountable-attention-and-publication","purpose":"Compete for useful attention without allowing demand, compression, generation, advertising, or delivery to manufacture warrant.","invariants":["Demand may create an assignment but never evidence.","A source statement remains attributable to its source until an authorized editorial act adopts a narrower newsroom claim.","No public surface may create a factual commitment not licensed by the article, its cited evidence, its uncertainty, or a declared editorial stance.","A manuscript is not publishable unless deterministic gates clear and the latest exact-manuscript independent editorial judgment accepts it.","Corrections, clarifications, updates, and retractions must propagate to every dependent headline, article, feed, card, sitemap, metadata record, and syndication surface that Koios controls.","Audience demand, attention, advertising, revenue, provider cost, and editorial warrant are recorded as distinct facts and never substituted for one another.","Newsroom learning may propose a replay, route review, observation period, or standards review from durable outcomes; it may not itself publish, execute the replay, alter a route, or amend law.","LLMs may produce prose, images, or bounded choices; deterministic code owns serialization, digests, admission, ledgers, and publication transitions.","A provider is selected by the cheapest route that satisfies the declared quality and evidence requirements; zero marginal price never waives those requirements.","No deployment target becomes authoritative without parity evidence, an accepted bilateral EVM effect seam, a rollback route, and an explicit cutover act.","A public privacy surface must describe the requests the exact publication artifact actually emits; suspended advertising or attention may not be described as active, and active third-party carriers may not be described as absent.","Advertising units, placements, provider requests, seller declarations, performance receipts, and revenue enter Koios only under provider-authored or provider-accepted evidence; Koios never invents ads.txt authority."],"derivedFrom":["dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/ietf-conformant-clickbait.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/accountable-attention.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/agentic-newsroom.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/claims-to-prose.md","dev/content/notes/2026/06/01/news-topology.md"],"enforcedBy":["src/researching/writing/editing/standards.mts","src/researching/writing/editing/liss-editorial.mts","src/management/newsroom-learning.mts","src/researching/writing/editing/publishing/managing/circulating/index.mts","src/administrating/deploying/static-shadow.mts","src/administrating/deploying/static-profile-parity.mts"]}

lib/law/editorial-product-commissions.json:
{"kind":"koios.editorial-product-commission-law","version":1,"invariants":["Audience demand, attention, advertising, and revenue may select and fund a commission; they never supply factual warrant.","Every factual commitment must remain within admitted source evidence regardless of product cost, length, or urgency.","Collapse awareness is an available editorial perspective, never a subject-admission condition or compulsory frame.","A shorter product narrows the promised reporting task; it never weakens attribution, correction, privacy, harm, or fabrication gates."],"productProfiles":{"service-utility":"service-brief/v1","entertainment-celebrity":"current-news-brief/v1","sports":"current-news-brief/v1","culture":"current-news-brief/v1","politics-power":"standard-news/v1","business-consumer":"standard-news/v1","technology-science":"standard-news/v1","environment":"standard-news/v1","investigations":"deep-report/v1"},"profiles":{"service-brief/v1":{"promise":"Answer one time-sensitive reader need accurately and directly from an authoritative source, with the operative date, eligibility, price, location, schedule, or action easy to find.","evidenceBudget":{"targetWords":{"minimum":300,"maximum":650},"minimumDistinctAssertions":4,"minimumPrimaryAssertions":3,"minimumIndependentSources":1,"maximumWordsPerAssertion":90,"minimumSections":1,"sectionPurposes":["give the direct answer and identify who, what, where, and when it applies","explain the supported steps, exceptions, deadlines, costs, or unresolved status"]},"writerPromptLaws":["Lead with the answer or operative change; do not make the reader excavate it from an essay.","Use exact dates, jurisdictions, eligibility conditions, prices, schedules, and instructions only as the admitted source states them.","Distinguish a current rule from a proposal, forecast, rumor, or prior-year practice.","Do not pad a service answer with a generic systems meditation."]},"current-news-brief/v1":{"promise":"Report one current public event quickly, engagingly, and in proportion to its stakes while preserving attribution, uncertainty, privacy, and correction readiness.","evidenceBudget":{"targetWords":{"minimum":300,"maximum":650},"minimumDistinctAssertions":4,"minimumPrimaryAssertions":2,"minimumIndependentSources":1,"maximumWordsPerAssertion":120,"minimumSections":1,"sectionPurposes":["establish what happened, to whom, where, and when","supply the most useful confirmed context and response","close on the next supported date, decision, release, contest, or unresolved fact"]},"writerPromptLaws":["Be lively without laundering rumor into fact or manufacturing conflict, intimacy, scandal, or certainty.","Attribute claims about relationships, health, private conduct, wrongdoing, or disputed statements to the exact admitted source.","Do not confuse publicity material, fan speculation, anonymous social posts, and independent reporting.","Give the audience the promised factual payoff; curiosity may organize the headline but may not replace the answer."]},"standard-news/v1":{"promise":"Report one consequential current development with corroboration, useful context, and visible attribution, while sizing the article to the evidence rather than manufacturing an essay.","evidenceBudget":{"targetWords":{"minimum":450,"maximum":850},"minimumDistinctAssertions":7,"minimumPrimaryAssertions":4,"minimumIndependentSources":2,"maximumWordsPerAssertion":100,"minimumSections":2,"sectionPurposes":["establish what happened, who is responsible, where and when it occurred, and the immediate consequence","give the most useful corroborated context, response, disagreement, deadline, or next development"]},"writerPromptLaws":["Lead with the current development and its consequence; do not begin with a universal thesis or generic systems frame.","Separate established fact, attributed statement, allegation, estimate, interpretation, and unresolved uncertainty.","Use only as much background and analysis as the admitted evidence can advance without repetition.","Represent meaningful response or contrary evidence carried by the packet, and close on the next supported development rather than an abstract meditation."]},"reported-analysis/v2":{"promise":"Explain one consequential current event through corroborated reporting, with interpretation visibly subordinate to the evidence.","evidenceBudget":{"targetWords":{"minimum":800,"maximum":1100},"minimumDistinctAssertions":15,"minimumPrimaryAssertions":10,"minimumIndependentSources":2,"maximumWordsPerAssertion":60,"minimumSections":3,"sectionPurposes":["establish the reported event, actors, place, time, and present consequence","advance corroborated details, institutional context, disagreement, and response","explain only evidence-licensed implications and close on the decisive unresolved status"]},"writerPromptLaws":["The event and its people, institutions, places, dates, quantities, documents, and decisions remain the article's spine.","Separate established fact, source allegation, expert interpretation, Koios analysis, and unresolved uncertainty.","Represent meaningful contrary evidence or response carried by the packet.","Use systems interpretation only where the admitted evidence licenses the connection."]},"deep-report/v1":{"promise":"Produce an original deep report or synthesis from multiple independent sources, primary records where available, contrary evidence, and explicit reporting gaps.","evidenceBudget":{"targetWords":{"minimum":1200,"maximum":1800},"minimumDistinctAssertions":22,"minimumPrimaryAssertions":12,"minimumIndependentSources":3,"maximumWordsPerAssertion":70,"minimumSections":4,"sectionPurposes":["state the finding, event, or question and the evidence on which it rests","show the documentary chronology, mechanisms, and accountable actors","test the account against contrary evidence, limitations, and responses","explain supported consequences and identify the next unresolved reporting target"]},"writerPromptLaws":["Do not claim originality merely because Koios combined sources; identify what the reporting actually establishes.","Prefer primary records and direct evidence, preserve chronology, and expose evidentiary gaps.","Represent the subject's response or the documented effort to obtain it for consequential criticism.","A deep report may be long only because its evidence and analysis advance, never because its framing repeats."]}}}

INDEPENDENT EDITOR REPORT:

## Editorial Assessment â€” reporting-source-1-for-trevor-winkfield-cheerfully-sinister-worlds

### Source and Assignment Review

The single admitted source is a Hyperallergic critical review (published 2026-07-17) of the exhibition "Trevor Winkfield: The Mermaid's Revenge - Paintings 1991-2001" at Tibor de Nagy gallery, 11 Rivington Street, Lower East Side, Manhattan, running through July 31. The source is genuine, dated, and contains concrete and attributable material: specific painting titles with years, gallery and address, physical dimensions, the reviewer's named characterizations of style and tone, and biographical facts traceable to specific evidence cards. The source is adequate to support a 300â€“650-word current-news-brief anchored in the exhibition event. The source layer is sound.

The assignment targets a culture news brief about this exhibition and its critical reception. The evidence budget â€” 20 claims, 300â€“650 words â€” is appropriate to the material. The assignment layer is sound.

### Deterministic Standards

The deterministic reading marks the manuscript publishable (no blocking gate failures) but flags 14 near-duplicate-proximity warnings across all three body sections and one demand-lens-missing-h2 warning. These warnings are substantive: the 14 near-duplicate flags correspond to genuine prose-level repetition visible in the manuscript text, not instrument noise. The gate layer is clear as a matter of deterministic processing, but the warnings describe real defects that editorial review must address.

### Critical Defects Found in Manuscript

**1. Pipeline claim-ID markers left in publication copy (publication-blocking)**

Every factual sentence in the body ends with unstripped internal markers, for example:
> "â€¦has been marked by a consistent engagement with the intersections of poetry and art [claim:trevor-winkfield-s-cheerfully-sinister-worlds:2, claim:trevor-winkfield-s-cheerfully-sinister-worlds:10]."

These identifiers appear in every paragraph of the body and also in the frontmatter `summary` field. In standard Markdown, bracket expressions not in hyperlink syntax render as literal text. A reader would see `[claim:trevor-winkfield-s-cheerfully-sinister-worlds:14, claim:trevor-winkfield-s-cheerfully-sinister-worlds:15]` inline. This is a publication-blocking defect; the manuscript has not been stripped of its editorial-traceability annotation layer before submission. Because the markers appear in 12 or more discrete body locations and in the frontmatter summary, this cannot be repaired by a small number of bounded text replacements â€” it requires a clean regeneration pass.

**2. Lede does not name the event (structural rule violation)**

The instructions require the very first sentence to name the event concretely: who, where, what. The first sentence is: "The artist Trevor Winkfield has long inhabited a dual identity as both a visual practitioner and a literary figure, producing works that operate with a unique, meticulous precision." This is a career-profile opener, not an event opener. Neither the exhibition title, the gallery, the address, nor the closing date appears anywhere in the manuscript body. The article is structured as a timeless career overview that could have been written at any point in Winkfield's career, with no news hook anchoring it to the current exhibition. A reader following a link from this article would have no idea that a specific show is open in Manhattan through July 31.

**3. Source citation placed after first factual claim (citation-is-precondition violation)**

The instructions state: "cite THE STORY as [Exact Story Title](its-exact-url) before making its first factual claim." The second sentence â€” "His career, which began in earnest while attending school in Leeds and later moving to New York in 1969" â€” is a concrete factual claim. The source citation first appears in the third sentence: "As documented in [Trevor Winkfield's Cheerfully Sinister Worlds]â€¦". Two sentences of factual content precede the citation, violating the precondition rule. The cited title matches the source exactly, which is correct; only the placement is wrong.

**4. Attribution strengthening of single reviewer's characterization**

The manuscript writes: "The resulting imagery is frequently described as cheerfully sinister, a duality that speaks to the artist's ability to imbue artificial settings with a sense of mysterious, if incomprehensible, activity."

The phrase "frequently described as" implies a critical consensus. The source establishes one reviewer's characterization: "He has conjured an artificial world â€” simultaneously brightly colored, slightly sinister, and cheerfully incomprehensible." This is one named publication's description of the work in one review. The manuscript strengthens the modality from a single source attribution to a recurring critical consensus without warrant. The claim should be attributed visibly to the Hyperallergic reviewer's language.

**5. Unattributed evaluative adjective**

The manuscript characterizes Winkfield as "an insightful writer, contributing to a body of criticism." The source says he has "written smart and original pieces." "Insightful" is the manuscript's own paraphrase of an evaluative quality, not the source's term, and appears without attribution.

**6. Near-duplicate proximity â€” 14 flagged instances**

The four sentences of the "Systems of Representation" section are particularly redundant. Each sentence introduces a variation on the same idea â€” Winkfield's resistance to interpretation, the viewer's engagement with artificial structures, the self-referential logic of the imagery â€” without advancing the argument. The "Meticulous Stylistic Logic" section similarly defines the palette in one sentence and then re-characterizes the same palette feature in the next two sentences. The "Connections to Literary Traditions" section describes his role as a writer in three consecutive sentences that partially overlap. These are not minor stylistic preferences; they inflate word count without adding licensed factual content, and they directly reflect the warning pattern flagged by the copy-editing gate.

**7. Frontmatter summary contains raw claim IDs**

The YAML `summary` field reads: "â€¦Winkfield's paintings are defined by a specific, saturated palette and a flat, volumetric style that eschews traditional depth in favor of a packed, illustrative surface [claim:trevor-winkfield-s-cheerfully-sinister-worlds:14, claim:trevor-winkfield-s-cheerfully-sinister-worlds:15]." This field is publication-facing (used in feed distribution and syndication per the pipeline configuration). Internal claim-ID markers in the summary field would surface in feeds and social cards.

### Evidence Audit â€” Material Claims Against Witnessed Source

Claims properly grounded in the witnessed evidence:
- Winkfield earned a master's degree from the Royal College of Art in 1967, moved to New York in 1969, published the poetry magazine Juillard (1968â€“72): supported by claim:2 and the source summary.
- Collaborated with poets John Ashbery, Charles North, Ron Padgett, Harry Matthews in 1976: supported by claim:6.
- Published translation of Raymond Roussel's *How I Wrote Certain of My Books* in 1977: supported by claim:7.
- Roussel wrote using homophones: supported by claim:8.
- Works on linen in acrylic; the exhibition contains eight pieces (1991â€“2001): supported by claim:12 and the source summary.
- Specific paintings "The Student" (1999), "The Navigator" (2000), "The Astrologer" (2001), "Self-Portrait" (2001): supported by claim:17.
- "The Student" figure detail (helmet, fish, lock, long-handled pot, lightbulb, snowflake tokens): supported by claim:19.
- Tokens reappear above a pink and pale-blue mountain in an open window: supported by claim:20.
- Writings collected in *Georges Braque and Others: The Selected Art Writings of Trevor Winkfield, 1990â€“2009* (2014): supported by claim:18.
- Worked for Arthur Cohen on Dada/Surrealism catalogs: supported by claim:3.

Claims that are over-stated or not adequately supported:
- "frequently described as cheerfully sinister" â€” overstates the single Hyperallergic reviewer's characterization as a critical consensus (as noted above).
- The manuscript says critics "searched for specific meanings within his paintings"; the source says critics "tried to connect Winkfield's collage-like paintings of artificial worlds with Roussel's wildly improbable novels." The manuscript paraphrase is broader than what claim:9 licenses.

### Pipeline Diagnosis

The failure layer is **writer-model**. The source and assignment are adequate to support the commission. The instructions are explicit on all violated rules (citation precondition, first-sentence event naming, claim-ID traceability as internal-only). The gate layer cleared on a deterministic reading but correctly flagged the near-duplicate proximity issues as warnings. The writer model (gemini-3.1-flash-lite) produced copy that: left internal pipeline traceability markers in publication-facing fields; structured the article as a career overview rather than an event news brief; placed the source citation after the first factual sentence; and padded the final section with near-duplicate restatements. These failures are intrinsic to the draft's architecture and cannot be resolved by bounded text-replacement repair â€” they require a clean writer-model pass with the same evidence cards and corrective instruction.

The headline ("Trevor Winkfield's Precision Paradox"), generated by a separate headline model, does not preserve the source event's organizing terms and introduces a frame not supported by the source. The headline should also be regenerated in the replay pass.

### Corrective Instructions for Replay

The replay should: (1) open the first sentence with the exhibition name, gallery, location, and dates; (2) place the Hyperallergic source link before the first factual claim; (3) attribute stylistic characterizations visibly to the Hyperallergic reviewer rather than presenting them as consensus; (4) strip claim-ID markers from all publication-facing fields before output; (5) have each body section add new concrete material (specific paintings, dimensions, specific writing titles) rather than restating the style/duality frame from the previous section; (6) not use "frequently described as" or equivalent consensus-implying language for single-source characterizations.


